{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "F20ConstantFoldedRhsLosesTheArrayShape",
    "description": "Finding F19. An elementwise equation whose right-hand side constant-folds to a SCALAR loses the left-hand side's declared array shape, and the variable then has no cells at all.\n\n`guarded` is declared over `row_ax` and its equation is `ifelse(zeroGuard > 0, col[i], 0.0)`. `zeroGuard` is a `parameter` whose default is 0.0, so the predicate is a compile-time false and the whole `ifelse` folds to the scalar literal 0.0. The intended value is a three-cell array of zeros -- an array assigned a scalar broadcasts, which is what `unguarded` below demonstrates on the same shape. What happens instead is that the variable is absent from the state map.\n\nThe control is `unguarded`, identical but with the guard's default at 1.0 so the fold does not collapse the branch; it materializes correctly. So the difference is the fold and not the shape, the `ifelse`, or the parameter.\n\nLOUD, not silent, which is what keeps this a cost rather than a hazard: `esm test` reports `array state 'guarded' has no cells in var_map` and names the variable.\n\nIMPACT, and it is narrow but real. It removes one testing technique: a component cannot exercise the FALSE arm of a guard whose predicate is a run-level scalar by overriding that scalar, which is the natural way to test a zero-denominator guard or a disabled adjustment. Both places this port wanted it, the technique had to be replaced by data: components/onroad_travel_fraction.esm's `share_of_group` guard is exercised by a probe ROW whose group total is zero rather than by overriding the carried denominator, and components/onroad_energy_output.esm's clamps are exercised by moving a temperature that both arms are reachable from rather than by forcing a factor to zero. Both replacements are better tests -- per-row data exercises the join as well as the arithmetic -- so this cost the port two rewrites and no capability.\n\nFIX SHAPE. Broadcast a scalar-folded right-hand side across the left-hand side's declared shape, which is what the same document already does when the fold does not collapse the branch. The array runtime knows the shape from the declaration; the folder is discarding it.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "finding",
      "constant-folding",
      "array-shape"
    ]
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "row_ax": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 3
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "F19ConstantFoldedRhsLosesTheArrayShape": {
      "variables": {
        "zeroGuard": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "A compile-time false predicate, so the `ifelse` below folds to the scalar 0.0."
        },
        "oneGuard": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "The control: a compile-time true predicate, so the fold keeps the array branch."
        },
        "col": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "row_ax"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "A three-cell array column."
        },
        "guarded": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "row_ax"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Declared over row_ax; its RHS folds to a scalar. Expected: three cells of 0.0."
        },
        "unguarded": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "row_ax"
          ],
          "units": "1",
          "description": "The control, identical but for the guard's value."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": "col",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "const",
            "args": [],
            "value": [
              10.0,
              20.0,
              30.0
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "guarded",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "ifelse",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": ">",
                "args": [
                  "zeroGuard",
                  0.0
                ]
              },
              "col",
              0.0
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "unguarded",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "ifelse",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": ">",
                "args": [
                  "oneGuard",
                  0.0
                ]
              },
              "col",
              0.0
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "a_scalar_folded_rhs_broadcasts_over_the_declared_shape",
          "description": "The intended behaviour, which is what makes this repro fail today. `unguarded` materializes and `guarded` does not, and the two differ only in whether the fold collapsed the branch. When this test starts passing, a component can once again exercise the false arm of a scalar-predicated guard by overriding the scalar.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "unguarded",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 10.0,
              "coords": {
                "row_ax": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "guarded",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "row_ax": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "guarded",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "row_ax": 3
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}